- Code/test commit: `cceed2ab feat(protocol): map IgnoreErrorGetter writer flag`.
  Documentation and execution-log updates are recorded separately.
- Mapped Fastjson2 `IgnoreNonFieldGetter`: oracle fixtures show it removes the
  three computed `QueueTimeSpan` timestamp strings, writes `MessageQueue` map
  keys as quoted compact JSON strings, and quotes numeric route-map keys.
  Rust applies the getter filter in the shared serializer and the custom body
  map-key serializer; fixture assertions cover body, route, and heartbeat DTOs.
- The first Rust compile required qualifying the shared JSON-string writer.
  The next comparison exposed that `QueryConsumeTimeSpanBody` uses the shared
  serializer, so filtering only the special body serializer left its three
  getter fields present. Moved the filter to the shared route serializer and
  reran the entire Protocol suite successfully.
- `cargo test -p rocketmq-classic-protocol --all-features --locked`: passed
